<InfoPage title="Privacy policy" description="Read the Metadata Remover privacy policy, including how browser-based processing, preferences, and support requests are handled.">
  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> August 24, 2026</p>
  <section><h2>Browser-based file processing</h2><p>Metadata Remover processes supported files locally in your browser. We do not upload files selected in the remover to our servers, and we do not retain copies of those files.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Information stored on your device</h2><p>We use your browser’s local storage to remember your selected theme. This preference stays in your browser until you clear site data or change the theme.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Information you send to us</h2><p>If you contact us at <a href="mailto:support@metadataremovertool.com">support@metadataremovertool.com</a>, we receive the information in your message and use it to respond, provide support, and protect the service.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Analytics and third-party services</h2><p>The site loads fonts from Google Fonts and uses Google Analytics to understand visits and general page interactions. Google Analytics may receive session statistics, approximate location, and browser or device information under Google’s own privacy practices. Advertising storage and personalization signals are disabled. For visitors in the European Economic Area, United Kingdom, and Switzerland, analytics storage defaults to denied through Google Consent Mode. We do not send selected file contents, filenames, detected metadata, or cleanup choices to Google Analytics.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You can stop using the service at any time, clear local storage through your browser settings, and choose not to send us information by email.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Contact and jurisdiction</h2><p>Metadata Remover operates from India. Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:support@metadataremovertool.com">support@metadataremovertool.com</a>.</p></section>
</InfoPage>
